{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445085-different-methods-of-crafting-by-different-people","id":1445085,"title":"Different methods of crafting by different people","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T11:52:46-07:00","id":1445085,"title":"Different methods of crafting by different people","content":"Ok I have Forged in Dragon's fire in front of me (metaphorically). <br /> <br /> Charms/ Gadgets are single-shot stuff: In other words, the bullets, the expendable charms, the grenades. <br /> <br /> Artifacts/ Inventions: Basically your run of the mill triggerable rote, requiring only 1 success to work. The equivalent of a ray gun, a magic wand, or etc. <br /> <br /> Wonders/ Devices: This, I am not quite sure. What's the exact difference between this class and artifacts/ inventions? As far as I can tell, it's that Wonders/ Devices are imbued with their own arete. <br /> <br /> And another thing: <br /> <br /> I keep seeing references to Devices not need expenditure of willpower to create, while Wonders need it. Thus Wonders are extremely personal and valuable to a mage, and can cast by themselves, while Devices require a mage to use it, but can be produced as long as you have the prime and materials to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:45:19-07:00","id":1445101,"title":"","content":"<u>Talismans/ Devices:</u> They are imbued with their own Arete, and that's a lot.<br /> <br /> *Under FbDF rules that allows a mage to use the Wonder even if he already casted an effect that turn. That's the only way of rolling Arete twice, effectively casting two effects, the same turn.<br /> <br /> *It also means normal ppl with the rigth training could use the item, while Artifacts/ Inventions can only be used by someone with Arete.<br /> <br /> There's a few other differences, but that's the biggest one.<br /> <br /> <u>Devices not needing expenditure of willpower to create:</u><br /> <br /> That's in Book of Secrets, if my memory isn't failing, it's an M20 upgrade. And it's only for technomancers with access to a Technocratic facility (if I'm not mistaken, how these facilities manage to waiver that cost it's currently unknown). Even a Technocrat will have to pay willpower to create a Device w/o access to these special facilities<br /> <br /> Devices can be used by normal people as easily, if not more, as Talismans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-21-2021, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:09:57-07:00","id":1445286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445085-different-methods-of-crafting-by-different-people?p=1445101#post1445101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Talismans/ Devices:</u> They are imbued with their own Arete, and that's a lot.<br /> <br /> *Under FbDF rules that allows a mage to use the Wonder even if he already casted an effect that turn. That's the only way of rolling Arete twice, effectively casting two effects, the same turn.<br /> <br /> *It also means normal ppl with the rigth training could use the item, while Artifacts/ Inventions can only be used by someone with Arete.<br /> <br /> There's a few other differences, but that's the biggest one.<br /> <br /> <u>Devices not needing expenditure of willpower to create:</u><br /> <br /> That's in Book of Secrets, if my memory isn't failing, it's an M20 upgrade. And it's only for technomancers with access to a Technocratic facility (if I'm not mistaken, how these facilities manage to waiver that cost it's currently unknown). Even a Technocrat will have to pay willpower to create a Device w/o access to these special facilities<br /> <br /> Devices can be used by normal people as easily, if not more, as Talismans</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thank you Aleph. But I also found another source. Technomancer's Toybox. Shouldn't have bothered you. <br /> <br /> But anyway, thanks. This actually clears up a lot of stuff about the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}